 class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/281160-promethean-dev-blog-alchemists-mixologists-of-fun?p=281417#post281417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh, now I'm picturing a Promethean farm created and managed by a firm of Alchemists. Long rows of Prometheans, locked in electrostasis containers and shocked/milked for Pyros. Any doubts the staff had about ethics have been utterly erased by collective Disquite along with sanity and inhibition. It's a bleak sight, made all the more gruesome by the warping of wasteland and increasingly unstable alchemical experiments. It's really only a matter of time before decay or a firestorm knocks out containment and unleashes a legion of furious, ignorant Prometheans into the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Parts: the Clonus Horror?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T13:41:53-07:00","id":281421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/281160-promethean-dev-blog-alchemists-mixologists-of-fun?p=281418#post281418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Parts: the Clonus Horror?</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T14:38:40-07:00","id":281487,"title":"","content":"Cannot help but remember Lorenzo from Hunting Grounds. That was a really scary mofo:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1N1E5QRw95g\" data-code=\"1N1E5QRw95g\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/1N1E5QRw95g/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> L: &quot;<i>Thy.... precioussss.... Azoth. &quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T14:45:48-07:00","id":281498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/281160-promethean-dev-blog-alchemists-mixologists-of-fun?p=281408#post281408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">following up on some things I\u2019ve said before: it seems to me that an alchemist ought to be able to perform the generative act the same way a Promeean does, providing he harvests a dot of Azoth in the form of Humour from an appropriate Promethean: take Choleric Humour from a Frankenstein and use it to create another Frankenstein. <b>No desperation needed</b>-</div> </div> </div> </div>I hate being the raincloud in the middle of a sunny day, I really do. I think most of you know how excited I get over things, and even if I'm not, I'm generally positive. I'm sorry this seems to be my blind spot.<br /> <br /> All that said, to this, I must say:<br /> <br /> LOL, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T15:06:10-07:00","id":281509,"title":"","content":"While I wouldn't restrict the generative act strictly to despiration, I will say that it should not be sanely possible. By this I mean, even if for only a moment, the Demiurge must be completely off his rocker. For most, that'd be because of desperation, but legendary hubris, mad certainty, and good old total insanity may also be viable.<br /> <br /> Basically, if the Demiurge is giving even passing consideration to the concept of repercussions, he should fail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 10-14-2014, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T15:19:03-07:00","id":281512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/281160-promethean-dev-blog-alchemists-mixologists-of-fun?p=281498#post281498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that said, to this, I must say:<br /> <br /> LOL, no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't get me wrong: I'm not saying that mortals using desperation to create Prometheans doesn't have a place. In fact, I think it has a very good place: someone who doesn't have access to Pyros or doesn't know that he needs it can <i>still</i> make a Promethean (or perform other acts of alchemy) through desperation; it provides a way for people to &quot;break the rules&quot; and do things they shouldn't be able to do. But making it the <i>only</i> way that mortals can create Prometheans closes down too many story possibilities, such as PenDragon's &quot;Promethean farm&quot;. Tying it to alchemists is not only thematically appropriate, but also keeps it from having no down-side: While no desperation would be needed, mutilation of another Promethean would be needed instead. That, or maybe harvesting Pyros from a Firestorm (which has the twin problems of Firestorms being unpredictable and very dangerous). <br /> <br /> Frankly, I'm not a big fan of the notion that mortals creating Prometheans is an almost-unheard-of thing. I have no problem with the creation of Prometheans being easier than 1e made it out to be, as long as it doesn't go to the other extreme of anyone being able to create a Promethean on a whim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T19:07:50-07:00","id":281805,"title":"","content":"Alchemists don't add much that wasn't already there; they're just a logical outgrowth of the setting's assumptions. While they may be the best candidates for mortal demiurges, that sort of thing is still best left to ST fiat, not to codified rules. I'm hoping for some rules and guidance on making alchemists interesting and discrete antagonists, but in all honesty, I'd prefer getting the Zeky as antagonists instead.<br /> <br /> Still, maybe the OP folks will pick up on the demand for actual alchemist PCs before long, though I'd rather see it stuck in a Second Sight Second Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T22:53:32-07:00","id":281975,"title":"","content":"While I'm a bit disappointed with the update, as it doesn't really tell us anything we couldn't infer from the previous mention of the Alchemists hunting Prometheans (which is why I voted for Refinements) - I'm on board from them getting full antagonist coverage in the 2nd edition core, provided it comes with actual formulae they wield. They should after all be more common than the... something like... <i><b>five </b></i>Zeky that exist at any given time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T06:36:32-07:00","id":282221,"title":"","content":"I'm vaguely tickled that the Zeky seem to have been kicked specifically for these guys, but I'm not certain exactly why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T06:57:57-07:00","id":282233,"title":"","content":"Can\u00b4t alchemists become partners or even the equivalent of ghouls for Prometheans (&quot;I will work for you in exchange of x supplus of mojo&quot;)? after all, the Created are tought preys to say at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T09:15:02-07:00","id":282349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/281160-promethean-dev-blog-alchemists-mixologists-of-fun?p=282221#post282221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm vaguely tickled that the Zeky seem to have been kicked specifically for these guys, but I'm not certain exactly why.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Zeky still have their old write up and they can always be properly updated in a later supplement, so I'm not too torn up about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T09:18:39-07:00","id":282352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/281160-promethean-dev-blog-alchemists-mixologists-of-fun?p=282233#post282233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can\u00b4t alchemists become partners or even the equivalent of ghouls for Prometheans (&quot;I will work for you in exchange of x supplus of mojo&quot;)? after all, the Created are tought preys to say at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only temporarily, I'd assume, with Disquiet and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T09:39:23-07:00","id":282397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Only temporarily, I'd assume, with Disquiet and all. </div> </div> </div>While difficult, it would be possible for them to keep a middle distance relationship, only meeting for important stuff. That would lessen the Disquiet\u00b4s erosion on the alchemist\u00b4s sanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T11:45:27-07:00","id":282556,"title":"","content":"Matt's said before that having a ghoul equivalent for Prometheans goes against the themes of the game. I largely agree with him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T12:16:56-07:00","id":282570,"title":"","content":"I feel differently. Promethian is about learning to be human, among other things, and if a theme is about 'students' there is always room for teachers.<br /> <br /> Even the original Frankenstein had the blind man who tutored the monster. The Golem and the Djinn (rivalling Frankenstein for most appropraite Promethian inspiration) had Rabbi Meyer. Pinocchio has Geppetto.<br /> <br /> In fact, it seems like every story about an artificial created being trying to learn humanity - whether they're rejected or accepted by mankind - has at least one mentor charachter. I'm fine with Disquiet, but I don't like the way Promethian locks out such a huge and thematically powerful part of the source material. I'd like to give alchemists an elixir to protect against disquiet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T12:34:31-07:00","id":282581,"title":"","content":"It doesn't, it just ties it into the group dynamic more.<br /> <br /> Besides, those people are exceptions. It's hard to make them feel exceptional when they're treated as a common part of the setting. The narrative should provide those sort of peoples, not mechanical templates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T14:14:31-07:00","id":282701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/281160-promethean-dev-blog-alchemists-mixologists-of-fun?p=282397#post282397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While difficult, it would be possible for them to keep a middle distance relationship, only meeting for important stuff. That would lessen the Disquiet\u00b4s erosion on <b>the alchemist\u00b4s sanity</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>*chuckle*<br /> <br /> Seriously though, I suspect that alchemists are going to end up being like <b>Changeling</b>'s fetches: designed specifically to serve as antagonists for the game's central characters, but used by the occasional enterprising gaming group as rivals and even grudging allies -- or even, in some cases, protagonists in their own right. Just don't forget the original intent: relations between Prometheans and alchemists are intended to be hostile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T14:48:30-07:00","id":282745,"title":"","content":"For some reason, I could not help but imagine a conversation between an Alchemist and one of the researches of Last Dynasty Inc from Mummy the Curse: <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;So you hunt seemingly immortal undead creatures that cause people to behave erratically? When you catch them you harvest seemingly miraculous substances from them to produce superhuman levels of ability in normal people. What did you call these creatures again? Prometheans? Hmmmm...dons't sound very Egyptian. Mmmm oh nothing dear boy, just muttering to myself. I don't suppose the term &quot;Arisen&quot; mean anything to you? No? Why do I ask? No reason really, just curious.&quot; </i> <br /> <br /> That's all before an Alchemist that has done a bit more research mentions Osirans, then things get even more confused. Leading to the inevitable argument of: <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;No its pronounced SEK-HEM, say it with me, SEK-HEM. No not Vitriol, that's so 19th century, trust me, I would know.&quot;</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T14:55:54-07:00","id":282752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/281160-promethean-dev-blog-alchemists-mixologists-of-fun?p=282745#post282745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some reason, I could not help but imagine a conversation between an Alchemist and one of the researches of Last Dynasty Inc from Mummy the Curse:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;So you hunt seemingly immortal undead creatures that cause people to behave erratically? When you catch them you harvest seemingly miraculous substances from them to produce superhuman levels of ability in normal people. What did you call these creatures again? Prometheans? Hmmmm...dons't sound very Egyptian. Mmmm oh nothing dear boy, just muttering to myself. I don't suppose the term &quot;Arisen&quot; mean anything to you? No? Why do I ask? No reason really, just curious.&quot; </i><br /> <br /> That's all before an Alchemist that has done a bit more research mentions Osirans, then things get even more confused. Leading to the inevitable argument of:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;No its pronounced SEK-HEM, say it with me, SEK-HEM. No not Vitriol, that's so 19th century, trust me, I would know.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>You can also add Cheiron Group to the mix:<br /> <br /> <i> Hey Alchemist, want to keep doing what you are doing and get paid?</i><br /> to the LDI member: <i> How much are they paying you?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T15:09:07-07:00","id":282763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/281160-promethean-dev-blog-alchemists-mixologists-of-fun?p=282570#post282570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel differently. Promethian is about learning to be human, among other things, and if a theme is about 'students' there is always room for teachers.<br /> <br /> Even the original Frankenstein had the blind man who tutored the monster. The Golem and the Djinn (rivalling Frankenstein for most appropraite Promethian inspiration) had Rabbi Meyer. Pinocchio has Geppetto.<br /> <br /> In fact, it seems like every story about an artificial created being trying to learn humanity - whether they're rejected or accepted by mankind - has at least one mentor charachter. I'm fine with Disquiet, but I don't like the way Promethian locks out such a huge and thematically powerful part of the source material. I'd like to give alchemists an elixir to protect against disquiet.</div> </div> </div> </div>My concern with an anti-Disquiet elixir is that it would tend to undermine the antagonistic relationship that the author is going for. The problem with an elixir that staves off Disquiet is that it can potentially mass-produced or shared. Now, if we were talking about <b>Hunter</b>\u2019s Ascended Ones, I\u2019d have less of a concern: given that they were conceived as protagonists, giving them a possible way around Disquiet falls under the \u201cfacilitating crossovers\u201d \u00e6gis; and given that their elixirs are poison to anyone but themselves and other Ascended Ones, introducing such an Elixir into their repertoire is unlikely to have further unintended consequences. <br /> <br /> More generally, I\u2019m not against the notion of there being a way for mortals to become immune to Disquiet, in much the same way that mages have Sleepwalkers and werewolves have Wolf-Blooded; but I feel that in general, it ought to be the sort of thing that\u2019s primarily in the Storyteller\u2019s hands, and/or something that comes at great cost to the person who gets the immunity. For instance:<br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Fire-Touched: one-dot Supernatural Merit</b><br /> Characters with this condition have encountered the Divine Fire and have come away with a touch of madness. Choose a Persistent Mental Condition that represents the insanity that you picked up from the Divine Fire. In any scene where that Condition might earn you a Beat, you may instead opt to lower one Disquiet Condition (if you have any) by one step, and to be exempt from rolls to resist Disquiet for the rest of that scene.</div><br /> The idea is to intrinsically link immunity to Disquiet with there being something wrong with the mortal in question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T11:19:26-07:00","id":285163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/281160-promethean-dev-blog-alchemists-mixologists-of-fun?p=282763#post282763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Fire-Touched: one-dot Supernatural Merit</b><br /> Characters with this condition have encountered the Divine Fire and have come away with a touch of madness. Choose a Persistent Mental Condition that represents the insanity that you picked up from the Divine Fire. In any scene where that Condition might earn you a Beat, you may instead opt to lower one Disquiet Condition (if you have any) by one step, and to be exempt from rolls to resist Disquiet for the rest of that scene.</div><br /> The idea is to intrinsically link immunity to Disquiet with there being something wrong with the mortal in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm okay with the concept, especially the idea that immunity to Disquiet is a sign of Problems, though the name Fire-Touched makes my Pure senses tingle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The penalties may be too bad to justify the cost, I feel. I get that it's supposed to be a major cost, but having to give up a chance for a beat and still not be totally immune doesn't seem worth the paper it's printed on. :/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T16:09:04-07:00","id":285480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/281160-promethean-dev-blog-alchemists-mixologists-of-fun?p=282701#post282701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously though, I suspect that alchemists are going to end up being like <b>Changeling</b>'s fetches: designed specifically to serve as antagonists for the game's central characters, but used by the occasional enterprising gaming group as rivals and even grudging allies -- or even, in some cases, protagonists in their own right. Just don't forget the original intent: relations between Prometheans and alchemists are intended to be hostile.</div> </div> </div> </div>This might be my favorite description of Alchemists in 2e thus far, and a near-perfect comparison. I do dig the idea that Alchemists represent the dark mirror of a Promethean's Pilgrimage, both seeking to better themselves while passing each other in opposite directions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T16:32:03-07:00","id":285489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/281160-promethean-dev-blog-alchemists-mixologists-of-fun?p=285163#post285163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm okay with the concept, especially the idea that immunity to Disquiet is a sign of Problems, though the name Fire-Touched makes my Pure senses tingle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>True. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/281160-promethean-dev-blog-alchemists-mixologists-of-fun?p=285163#post285163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The penalties may be too bad to justify the cost, I feel. I get that it's supposed to be a major cost, but having to give up a chance for a beat and still not be totally immune doesn't seem worth the paper it's printed on. :/</div> </div> </div> </div>My thought here was that you\u2019re effectively buying a scene\u2019s-worth (or maybe chapter\u2019s-worth?) of immunity to Disquiet for one Beat: not so much giving up a chance for a beat as using that beat to get something useful. But the essence of it is what I was trying to get across; the specific mechanics would need to be hammered out by the development team.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T04:24:07-07:00","id":288454,"title":"","content":"Hmm, well the text specifically mentioned that the alchemists tend to metaphorically carve out pieces of their humanity in their quest to become something better. <br /> <br /> Keeping in the no such thing as a free lunch theme to alchemists, a potion to remove disquiet would be a chemical lobotomy. <br /> <br /> Or as a plot point, perhaps this presumably well meaning alchemist's cure protects the alchemist by deadening their emotions, leaving their ally or contact temporarily less human than they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T08:00:16-07:00","id":288538,"title":"","content":"Since I'm using a phone right now and can't link to spoilers:<br /> <br /> Given how the Pristine Order's byline is &quot;POOR PEOPLE! AAAAAAHHHH!&quot;, I get the sense most alchemists aren't serious transhumanists anyway. A real believer (besides not liking sugar on his porridge) would be a philanthropist lifting other alchemists up to their level rather than killing anyone who dares threaten the self-image of old money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 10-21-2014, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T15:44:59-07:00","id":289027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/281160-promethean-dev-blog-alchemists-mixologists-of-fun?p=282570#post282570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel differently. Promethian is about learning to be human, among other things, and if a theme is about 'students' there is always room for teachers.<br /> <br /> Even the original Frankenstein had the blind man who tutored the monster. The Golem and the Djinn (rivalling Frankenstein for most appropraite Promethian inspiration) had Rabbi Meyer. Pinocchio has Geppetto.<br /> <br /> In fact, it seems like every story about an artificial created being trying to learn humanity - whether they're rejected or accepted by mankind - has at least one mentor charachter. I'm fine with Disquiet, but I don't like the way Promethian locks out such a huge and thematically powerful part of the source material. I'd like to give alchemists an elixir to protect against disquiet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Scions are a thing. You can always have such a character as the child of a Promethean or, if you twist the concept just a little bit, as a descendant who is a Scion due to atavism. So yea, this has always been possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","name":"Ravraxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T16:39:09-07:00","id":289094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravraxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/281160-promethean-dev-blog-alchemists-mixologists-of-fun?p=289027#post289027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scions are a thing. You can always have such a character as the child of a Promethean or, if you twist the concept just a little bit, as a descendant who is a Scion due to atavism. So yea, this has always been possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, never heard of those Scions - once more I point out I read most of corebook and saw some parts in <b>Magnum Opus</b> only, so they probably were elsewere in the gameline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T16:41:48-07:00","id":289095,"title":"","content":"They're in Magnum Opus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T18:55:45-07:00","id":289157,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll note that most (all?) of what is in Magnum Opus was \u201csetting hacks\u201d in 1e. 2e is importing some material from that book and making it \u201cofficial\u201d (e.g., the additional Refinements and the Extempore); but much of the book\u2019s material is still \u201csetting hacks\u201d \u2014 though exactly what is and isn\u2019t will remain murky until we see more of 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T05:15:43-07:00","id":289450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Dataweaver:</b> Seriously though, I suspect that alchemists are going to end up being like Changeling's fetches: designed specifically to serve as antagonists for the game's central characters, but used by the occasional enterprising gaming group as rivals and even grudging allies -- or even, in some cases, protagonists in their own right. Just don't forget the original intent: relations between Prometheans and alchemists are intended to be hostile. </div> </div> </div>That sounds right (as it happens, I prefer the non-hostile relationships between changelings and fetches, but I figure I'll be the opposite when it comes to alchemists). But I also wonder if they'll become the new Pure, with a cadre of fans who insist they should be the true protagonists no matter how evil they get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T05:22:48-07:00","id":290449,"title":"","content":"Will alchemist get their own formulae, or simply adapt Promethean\u00b4s refinements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T05:39:04-07:00","id":290452,"title":"","content":"I only hope than an Alchemist has the capability to Jekyll themselves into a Hyde form - and I'm not talking about movie gorilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T08:34:46-07:00","id":292979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/281160-promethean-dev-blog-alchemists-mixologists-of-fun?p=288538#post288538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since I'm using a phone right now and can't link to spoilers:<br /> <br /> Given how the Pristine Order's byline is &quot;POOR PEOPLE! AAAAAAHHHH!&quot;, I get the sense most alchemists aren't serious transhumanists anyway. A real believer (besides not liking sugar on his porridge) would be a philanthropist lifting other alchemists up to their level rather than killing anyone who dares threaten the self-image of old money.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, Lel, that's an illogical assumption, assuming that the pristine order is representative of alchemists, when they are a white, male, old money evil country club type of group, unless there is a reason to believe that alchemists scew towards old money, white, and male, and since they have their underwear in a bunch about &quot;poor people gasp&quot; using alchemy, that's probably not the case.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T09:44:18-07:00","id":293001,"title":"","content":"Well, alchemists _have_ historically skewed towards male and old money, and, in the West, white.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T10:16:47-07:00","id":293029,"title":"","content":"As long as you\u2019re comfortable with saying that \u201cwhite\u201d includes germans, frenchmen, italians, spaniards\u2026 But yeah, alchemists have traditionally <i>needed</i> to be affluent (which in turn generally translates to \u201cold money\u201d, since upward mobility tended to be rare until relatively recently), and tended to be male.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T11:09:55-07:00","id":293069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As long as you\u2019re comfortable with saying that \u201cwhite\u201d includes germans, frenchmen, italians, spaniards\u2026 </div> </div> </div>Who are white? Only anglos? I supose I would be branded &quot;latino&quot; if I where ever near the States, but germans are not white? Like, for real? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, shouldn't it be <i>Spanish</i>? Spaniards is... weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T11:23:06-07:00","id":293076,"title":"","content":"What about Chinese? Alchemy has also a long history on the East; just yesterday I watched a documentary about Emperor Quin Shi Huang, and how he sent Taoist alchemist Xu Fu in the company of 1000 men and women to the sea to find the Elixir of Life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 10-26-2014, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T12:06:57-07:00","id":293112,"title":"","content":"White is a storied and problematic word, and probably not the best one for the discussion, but in the US, it still describes the likely suspects. In Europe, you're still looking at descendents of nobility and established mercantile dynasties, most of which would &quot;pass&quot; over here, and wouldn't challenge the order the Auric Chalice wants to preserve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T13:52:44-07:00","id":293171,"title":"","content":"\u201cThe West\u201d is also a storied and problematic term, and also not particularly germane to the discussion. The point is that this particular faction draws most of its membership from the privileged elite, whoever they happen to be in whatever society you happen to be talking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T21:33:34-07:00","id":293383,"title":"","content":"Oh, DW, you see the pristine order as having world wide membership? As they are described I don't really see someone descended from the court alchemists of China fitting in, or those whose family have been practicing alchemy in Egypt since before the pyramids were built, I'd expect them to have their own organizations, who might very well be embodiments of every negative stereotype of the 1% as well, obnoxious in different ways, or not as obnoxious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T22:02:26-07:00","id":293396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/281160-promethean-dev-blog-alchemists-mixologists-of-fun?p=293383#post293383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh, DW, you see the pristine order as having world wide membership? As they are described I don't really see someone descended from the court alchemists of China fitting in, or those whose family have been practicing alchemy in Egypt since before the pyramids were built, I'd expect them to have their own organizations, who might very well be embodiments of every negative stereotype of the 1% as well, obnoxious in different ways, or not as obnoxious.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose all these branches have an aristocratic lineage, given the expense of the materials and the need of a classical education. And to redeem my &quot;West&quot; statement, these were all the marks of the upper classes. It's only been in the last century that we've seen a democratization of education, such that the underclasses have an opportunity for college or university. Only in the last decade that olde alchemical texts might be digitized and available for distribution via JStor and other repositories. It's this sort of revolution that would create enough upset that the Chalice would see a need to take action. <br /> <br /> I don't have enough experience with Egyptian, Greek, Middle Eastern, Indian, or Chinese higher education or aristocracy to hazard whether there's an academic tradition that reveres native alchemical paradigms while intersecting with the upper crust. In these cases too, there's the specter of colonialism, which may have interrupted these lineages. As such, I tend to look at the Chalice as being Old Europe, New England, Antebellum South, and South American aristocrats. Whereas I believe Chinese alchemists will have more of a Taoist bent, at odds with the Confucianism of the noble traditions and the legalism(?) of the Party. <br /> <br /> I have no insight elsewhere. But why does Indian alchemy never get a mention?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T06:29:40-07:00","id":293691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>StSword:</b> Oh, DW, you see the pristine order as having world wide membership? As they are described I don't really see someone descended from the court alchemists of China fitting in, or those whose family have been practicing alchemy in Egypt since before the pyramids were built </div> </div> </div>Agreed. The nature of the organisation is (from what we've seen) such that it would never accept members from such backgrounds no matter how elite they might be in their own societies. I could totally see near identical groups forming in China, or India, or Japan, or the Middle East, and so on, but they too would be too self-entitled to accept those from outside their own conception of the elite. (It means the group can be used as a template for groups from other societies, but they won't be the <i>same</i> group - cf the arguments I always make about non-western covenants in Vampire).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T01:31:18-07:00","id":294614,"title":"","content":"Oh I had a thought about alchemists.<br /> <br /> I imagine alchemists are probably more likely than a normal schlub to know about torment, disquiet, and wasteland effects, I imagine an alchemist who doesn't want to tap a promethean like a beer keg avoids them like the bubonic plague, making non antagonistic alchemists naturally irrelevant to promethean games.<br /> <br /> So for every antagonist there might be an alchemist in medical school trying to cure cancer, but unless that guy wants to include powdered prometheans in the ingredient list he just isn't relevant to the game.<br /> <br /> Anyone else want to use alchemists in non promethean games? I mean obviously the promethean core book is going to be about prometheans, but I can see alchemists organically showing up in vampire, mage, changeling, hunter, geist, mummy, or demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T00:36:33-07:00","id":296725,"title":"","content":"Could Alchemists get Pyros from Pandorans? that might be a hook to allow an Alchemist and a Promethean to work together rather then become enemies. Help getting rid of dangerous monsters (good for the Created) AND a sours of Pyros (good for the human).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3857-kingme1","name":"Kingme1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T10:38:08-07:00","id":297225,"title":"","content":"If Pandorans are anything like they are in 1e, I doubt that that would work: a reason why Pandorans enter Dormancy when Prometheans aren\u2019t around is that they get the Pyros they need to remain active from Prometheans; so taking Pyros from a Pandoran <i>is</i> taking Pyros from a Promethean; just indirectly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T16:18:40-07:00","id":297581,"title":"","content":"Which is why a clever alchemist might keep a few Pandorans around on a leash.<br /> <br /> (that'll probably end well)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T22:58:18-07:00","id":297849,"title":"","content":"Do pandorans not turn back to stone or whatever when only humans are around anymore?<br /> <br /> I would think that putting a pandoran in a box and moving it around until the box starts moving is a way to find prometheans if you don't have a better way. <br /> <br /> Just you know, make sure its a sturdy box.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T17:39:39-08:00","id":300573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/281160-promethean-dev-blog-alchemists-mixologists-of-fun?p=282763#post282763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, if we were talking about <b>Hunter</b>\u2019s Ascended Ones, I\u2019d have less of a concern: given that they were conceived as protagonists, giving them a possible way around Disquiet falls under the \u201cfacilitating crossovers\u201d \u00e6gis; and given that their elixirs are poison to anyone but themselves and other Ascended Ones, introducing such an Elixir into their repertoire is unlikely to have further unintended consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to point this out - the Ascended Ones <i>do</i> have an Elixir that helps them out against Disquiet.<br /> <br /> Namely, they are slightly less likely to develop Disquiet, and they can spend Willpower to reduce Disquiet from stage 4 to stage 3, both in themselves and in people they interact with.<br /> <br /> I dunno how relevant that particular Elixir (Gentle Heart, Mortal Remains p. 29) will help out in the new edition, but there is precedent.<br /> <br /> And I have a feeling there will be some cross-bleeding between the Ascended Ones and Alchemists, at least on the thematic level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T00:04:03-08:00","id":300814,"title":"","content":"Thematically the AO and the alchemists probably have little in common.<br /> <br /> The AO doesn't include alchemists, if an AO wants to learn something new, they have to find someone who knows alchemy and beg, borrow, or steal the knowledge from them. The AO are cooks with a cook book, and the goals of the two groups are different too: self improvement versus monster hunting. Swordsmen versus blacksmith, computer user versus computer programmer.<br /> <br /> Now I imagine nothing stops an alchemist from hunting, especially for ingredients I imagine, but the end result probably wouldn't look too much like AO in details. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}